  "text": "Using a combination of wheel-thrown and figurative vessels, Jacob creates bodies of work that are heavily influenced by his cultural background and heritage. Fired in his soda gas kiln, his pieces display a wide range of deep colours and rich surface textures. Jacob transforms London’s construction clay using the kilns he built himself. The introduction of this waste material has brought new and distinctive surface finishes to his work, particularly through the unpredictable nature of soda firing. Within the figurative elements of his work, he incorporates pieces of natural slate and broken pottery collected from Britain’s coastlines and mountain ranges. These materials symbolise his Western heritage and express his cultural journey in a physical and creative form. For further information on pricing and availability for Jacob’s work, please contact info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk Artworks Chess Set by Jacob Chan Sake Set by Jacob Chan Ginger Jar by Jacob Chan Sake Bottle by Jacob Chan Ginger Jar by Jacob Chan Sake Bottle by Jacob Chan Sake Cups by Jacob Chan Teapot by Jacob Chan Back to Artists Bespoke Commissions Golden Earth Studio offers a bespoke commission service that utilises the construction byproducts of our clients’ homes. To explore the possibilities of commissioning a unique piece of artwork to compliments your interior space, get in touch via our contact form or email. info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk First & Last Name Email Phone Message Send",
